  "hints": [
    "XOR combines bits without carrying; AND identifies carry-producing positions.",
    "Shift carry bits left and repeat, masking to 32 bits so negative Python values terminate.",
    "While carry: a,b = a^b, ((a&b)<<1)&mask. Decode a as signed after the loop.",
    "Each iteration moves unresolved carry bits left. After at most 32 shifts, the masked representation is the exact signed sum."
  ],
  "editorial": "Use a 32-bit representation, sufficient for the input and output range. XOR computes the carry-free sum, and shifted AND computes carries. Mask carries to prevent Python sign extension from propagating indefinitely. Decode a negative result using complement operations, with no addition or subtraction in the reference. The oracle uses ordinary integer addition; separate AST regression checks audit the reference restriction.",
